<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Meat Board posts full-yr profit of NZ$3.4 mln.</title>
<headline>NZ Meat Board posts full-yr profit of NZ$3.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Meat Board said on Wednesday it recorded a net profit of NZ$3.4 million in the year to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Chief executive Neil Taylor said higher than expected levy income helped contribute to the surplus.</p>
<p>&quot;This was brought about by increased numbers of sheep and cattle being processed during the year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said the levy income was forecast to fall by about $1.6 million for the coming year.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
